From 5a9ca7d41dfcd98abe024c6cdb4ae6571751b8b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 18:14:27 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Tests compared to reference solutions

The tests of the three cases only checked that the computations ran: a
wrong result, for instance a null stress field, passed. They now compare
values of the output files, through cmake/run-and-check.py (Python 3,
standard library only; without Python 3, the cases are only run):

- polycrystal: one time step of 0.2 s (instead of 0.1 s), the axial stress
  Szz being compared to the one of Cast3M (results/polycrystal_cast3m.csv),
  relative tolerance of 1 % (difference 7.6e-5);
- cermet: two time steps of 0.2 s (instead of one of 0.4 s), Szz at 0.2 s
  and 0.4 s compared to Cast3M (results/cermet_cast3m.csv), 1 %
  (differences 0.16 % and 0.29 %);
- bubble: the stress at the bubble compared to the analytical hoop stress
  at the surface of the cavity, half the pressure, 20 % for the coarse mesh
  of the test (difference 16 %).

Each test writes its own output file (the bubble tests share theirs and
are serialized). The GPU variants give the same values as on the CPU.
